<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="diffeq-act-13" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>🏫 Activity 13 - Exploring Parameters </title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      This activity is due at the beginning of class on <alert>Monday, October 26</alert>. Please write all solutions on this sheet. If you need additional space, you may attach additional work to this sheet, but please clearly label your work with its corresponding problem. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        The electric potential in an LRC circuit is modeled by <md> E(t) = L \deriv{^2 q}{t^2} + R \deriv{q}{t} + \frac{1}{C} q. </md> This model uses the charge in the circuit <m>q</m> as the dependent variable. We use <m>L,R,C</m> to denote the inductance, resistance, and capacitance of the inductor, resistor, and capacitor in the circuit respectively.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task workspace="0.25in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Write the equation of motion for a damped harmonic osciallator, as seen in lecture. 
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Compare and contrast the models. What similarities do you notice? 
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Build a <m>(R,C)</m>-space diagram for this equation when <m>E(t) = 0</m> in the axes provided. Follow the same procedure that we used on the damped harmonic oscillator in class. 
        </p>
        <image source="images/blankQ1axes.jpg" width="40%">
          <shortdescription>A blank set of (t,P) axes. </shortdescription>
        </image>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Consider the differential equation <md> \deriv{y}{x} = e^{-0.01xy^2}. </md>
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task workspace="0.25in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Identify the slope function for this equation.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
           Find a general form for contours of the system.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Explain why this system has no equilibrium. 
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Consider the slope field for a linear ODE shown below. 
      </p>
      <image source="images/slope_field.png" width="50%">
        <shortdescription>A slope field.</shortdescription>
      </image>
    </introduction>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Identify at least 2 non-zero contours by sketching them on the slope field.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    

    <task >
      <statement>
        <p>
          Suppose the system has the initial condition that <m>y(-2) = 1</m>. Sketch the corresponding trajectory on the slope field. 
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find all equilibria for the system. Classify each of them as stable, unstable, or neither. Justify your answers. 
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
